# SCSS and Styling Conventions

The site is a dark-only design system matching sflgbtbowl.com. `CLAUDE.md` (Bootstrap and Theme Management) is the source of truth for the conventions below and for the tests that enforce them.

## SCSS Architecture

- [src/scss/_bootstrap-variables.scss](mdc:src/scss/_bootstrap-variables.scss) - Palette tokens (`$night*`, `$ink*`, `$pride-*`) and fonts
- [src/scss/sfggc-bootstrap.scss](mdc:src/scss/sfggc-bootstrap.scss) - Which Bootstrap components are compiled in (opt-in; check it before assuming a class has styles)
- [src/scss/sfggc.scss](mdc:src/scss/sfggc.scss) - Global styles and the `--sfggc-*` custom properties on `:root`
- Component-specific `.module.scss` files for scoped styles

## CSS Custom Properties

Use the `--sfggc-` prefix. `--bs-*` does not exist in this project.

```scss
.Card {
  background: var(--sfggc-night-mid);
  color: var(--sfggc-ink);
  border: 1px solid var(--sfggc-hairline);
}
```

Tokens: `--sfggc-night`, `-night-mid`, `-night-deep` (surfaces), `--sfggc-ink`, `-ink-dim` (text), `--sfggc-pride-red|orange|yellow|green|blue|purple` (accents). Every `var(--sfggc-*)` must resolve to a defined variable.

## Responsive Design Pattern

Mobile-first with Bootstrap breakpoints (576, 768, 992, 1200px):

```scss
.component {
  font-size: 1rem;            // mobile default

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
}
```

## Section Pattern (content pages)

A `section-heading` bar with a `section-panel` body directly beneath it (`section-panel` is a `surface-card` with the padding, flat top corners and missing top border that continue the heading):

```jsx
<section className={`${styles.Name} my-5`}>
  <h3 className="section-heading">Title</h3>
  <div className="section-panel">...</div>
</section>
```

## Typography

- Headings (h1-h3, `.display`) use Bungee; body text uses Inter
- Use `clamp()` for fluid headline sizes so wide Bungee words wrap on phones

## Do Not

- Use light-surface utilities (`bg-white`, `bg-light`, bare `text-dark`) or the retired light-theme palette; add a `theme-exempt` comment with a reason if truly needed
- Write inline hex colors in components; use the tokens
- Reference a `styles.Name` class that the module does not define (it renders as the string `undefined`)

## Images

- Use responsive images; store them in [src/images/](mdc:src/images/) by category
- For text over an image, add a gradient overlay in the component's own module styles
